                    {
                        "sense_id": "824a6415-32c6-3643-b6bf-21e9046944eb",
                        "entry_id": "67784a0b-2e6e-35fe-a7e6-d029b24bc333",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Teneur globale en lipides du sang."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b32e58b2-44ac-4bc6-bc7d-ee3cf25f7aae",
                                "sense_id": "824a6415-32c6-3643-b6bf-21e9046944eb",
                                "text": "Plusieurs études ont montré que si on augmente la lipidémie à l'aide d'un régime hautement énergétique, il est possible d'améliorer la survie et de retarder la dégénérescence des motoneurones chez les malades atteints de SLA (sclérose latérale amyotrophique)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7cc7e2fd-6565-320b-8313-8af45d96e9ea",
                        "entry_id": "67784a0b-2e6e-35fe-a7e6-d029b24bc333",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Teneur excessive en lipides du sang."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cc380f2-be8a-4fda-838e-896bd8780dd3",
                                "sense_id": "7cc7e2fd-6565-320b-8313-8af45d96e9ea",
                                "text": "Les facteurs de risque biologiques de l’hypertension, de l’obésité et de la lipidémie sont aussi des facteurs de risque solidement établis de cardiopathie coronarienne, d’accident vasculaire cérébral et de diabète."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36218931-565b-4ed5-b3dc-f4ce20b4b17a",
                        "source_entry_id": "67784a0b-2e6e-35fe-a7e6-d029b24bc333",
                        "target_lang_word": "lipemia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lipemia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8208d2d7-e5a3-3d7c-b733-9cac5669de06",
                                        "entry_id": "e063737c-a643-3ac8-b464-7ce213276332",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An excess of lipids or lipoproteins in the blood."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18306d79-f50e-4704-aee7-a3920dee1930",
                                                "sense_id": "8208d2d7-e5a3-3d7c-b733-9cac5669de06",
                                                "text": "The absence of lipemia in the 28 cases undergoing treatment, although many of them were severe, is a striking fact, and probably to be accounted for by the partial or complete fasting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f02a5993-cad5-4223-b8cc-e55293264c99",
                                                "sense_id": "8208d2d7-e5a3-3d7c-b733-9cac5669de06",
                                                "text": "The studies cited above do not permit a decision as to whether the observed lipemias represent a direct action of estrogen or whether the effect is mediated through another organ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6468a81e-095e-483a-80bb-4254af02c105",
                                                "sense_id": "8208d2d7-e5a3-3d7c-b733-9cac5669de06",
                                                "text": "In patients with increased platelet aggregation, fat-loading produced a somewhat higher degree of lipemia than in the normal volunteers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82c9db88-d90e-4169-9044-f045226593b4",
                                                "sense_id": "8208d2d7-e5a3-3d7c-b733-9cac5669de06",
                                                "text": "It is important to note that Lipemia can also be seen as an artifact when a blood sample is collected from a pet that has just recently eaten. In general, a fast of 12 hours is recommended to eliminate postprandial lipemia. If lipemia persists greater than 12 hours, the patient should be evaluated for diseases that may produce altered fat metabolism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
